includes.hero/search.html:
{%- comment -%}
  HERO SEARCH BAR — single source. HOME heroes only (never sub-pages).
  data.search_placeholder = the placeholder string.
  The magnifier icon is the canonical search glyph (locked).
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign h = include.data -%}
<div class="wiki-hero-search">
  <span class="wiki-hero-search-icon">{% if h.search_icon_inc %}{% capture sf %}hero/{{ h.search_icon_inc }}.html{% endcapture %}{% include {{ sf }} %}{% elsif h.search_icon %}{{ h.search_icon }}{% else %}<svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><circle cx="11" cy="11" r="8"/><path d="m21 21-4.35-4.35"/></svg>{% endif %}</span>
  <input class="wiki-hero-search-input" placeholder="{{ h.search_placeholder }}" />
</div>

includes.hero/spotlight.html:
{%- comment -%}
  HERO SPOTLIGHT · treatment 1 — CALL-TO-ACTION CARD (the Cantina / iPhone style).
  Single source. Goes in the hero aside. Edit once → propagates everywhere.
  data:
    eyebrow? · title (req) · desc?
    tags?      -> list of strings
    cta  (REQUIRED) -> button label (the call to action — every CTA card has one);
                       cta_href? makes it a link instead of a button
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign s = include.data -%}
<div class="wiki-hero-spotlight{% if s.class %} {{ s.class }}{% endif %}">
  {%- if s.eyebrow -%}<div class="wiki-hero-spotlight-eyebrow">{{ s.eyebrow }}</div>{%- endif -%}
  {%- if s.art_inc -%}{% capture af %}hero/{{ s.art_inc }}.html{% endcapture %}{% include {{ af }} %}{%- elsif s.art -%}{{ s.art }}{%- endif -%}
  <h3 class="wiki-hero-spotlight-title">{{ s.title }}</h3>
  {%- if s.desc -%}<p class="wiki-hero-spotlight-desc">{{ s.desc }}</p>{%- endif -%}
  {%- if s.tags -%}<div class="wiki-hero-spotlight-tags">{%- for t in s.tags -%}<span class="wiki-hero-spotlight-tag">{{ t }}</span>{%- endfor -%}</div>{%- endif -%}
  {%- if s.cta -%}{%- if s.cta_href -%}<a class="wiki-hero-spotlight-cta" href="{{ s.cta_href }}">{{ s.cta }}</a>{%- else -%}<button class="wiki-hero-spotlight-cta">{{ s.cta }}</button>{%- endif -%}{%- endif -%}
</div>

includes.hero/stats.html:
{%- comment -%}
  HERO STATS GRID — single source for the 1×4 key-numbers band.
  Used by any hero (home + sub-page). Always exactly 4 cells (canon).
  data = a list of { num, label }.
  Edit this file once → every hero's stat grid updates everywhere.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign stats = include.data -%}
<div class="wiki-hero-stats">
  {%- for s in stats -%}<div class="wiki-hero-stat"><div class="wiki-hero-stat-num"{% if s.color %} style="color:{{ s.color }}"{% endif %}>{{ s.num }}</div><div class="wiki-hero-stat-label">{{ s.label }}</div></div>{%- endfor -%}
</div>

includes.sections/catalog-section.html:
{%- comment -%}
  CATALOG SECTION  (a page-section type — the framing, not the visual)
  --------------------------------------------------------------------
  This is the chrome a contributor gets the moment they drop a "Catalog
  section" onto a page, BEFORE they pick what fills it:
    · the locked eyebrow  ("Full Catalog" + the list icon)   — top-left
    · the auto-derived summary ("40 drinks · 9 categories")  — top-right
    · an optional footnote                                    — bottom
    · a SLOT that holds the chosen VISUAL (today: the catalog list;
      tomorrow, any list-style visual — it's routed through the dispatcher)
  The summary VALUES are derived from whatever visual's data sits in the
  slot (total items + category count), so the count is always truthful and
  the contributor never types it. `unit` (default "item") sets the noun.

  Usage:  {% include sections/catalog-section.html data=page.catalog %}
  Data shape: title, unit?, visual?, tone?, footnote?, categories[] …
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign data = include.data -%}
{%- assign visual = data.visual | default: 'catalog' -%}
{%- assign unit = data.unit | default: 'item' -%}
{%- assign ncats = data.categories | size -%}
{%- assign total = 0 -%}
{%- for c in data.categories -%}{%- assign s = c.items | size -%}{%- assign total = total | plus: s -%}{%- endfor -%}
<section class="wiki-section catalog" data-tone="{{ data.tone | default: 'b' }}">
  <div class="wiki-section-inner">
    <div class="cat-head">
      <div>
        <div class="wiki-section-eyebrow">{% include icon.html name="list-ordered" %} Full Catalog</div>
        <h2 class="wiki-section-title">{{ data.title }}</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="cat-summary">{{ total }} {{ unit }}{% if total != 1 %}s{% endif %} &middot; {{ ncats }} categor{% if ncats == 1 %}y{% else %}ies{% endif %}{% if data.note %} &middot; {{ data.note }}{% endif %}</div>
    </div>

    {%- comment -%} the slot: route the chosen visual + its data through the dispatcher {%- endcomment -%}
    {% include visual.html type=visual data=data %}

    {%- if data.footnote -%}<div class="cat-footnote">{{ data.footnote }}</div>{%- endif -%}
  </div>
</section>

includes.sections/config-section.html:
{%- comment -%}
  CONFIG SECTION (a page-section type — the framing, not the chart).
  The chrome a contributor gets on dropping a "Config section":
    · locked eyebrow "Configurations" + the locked hard-drive icon
    · a required H2 heading (contributor-named)
    · optional intro paragraphs
    · the chart (the visual) in the slot
    · an optional footer spec line
  Contained (not full-bleed). Usage:
    {% include sections/config-section.html data=page.config %}
  Data: heading (req), intro?[], footer?, tone?, visual?, chart_title, items[]
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign data = include.data -%}
{%- assign visual = data.visual | default: 'config' -%}
<section class="wiki-section config" data-tone="{{ data.tone | default: 'a' }}" id="cfg-section">
  <div class="wiki-section-inner">
    <div class="wiki-section-eyebrow">{% include icon.html name="hard-drive" %} Configurations</div>
    <h2 class="wiki-section-title" style="margin-bottom:24px;">{{ data.heading }}</h2>
    {%- if data.intro -%}<div class="cfg-prose">{%- for p in data.intro -%}<p>{{ p }}</p>{%- endfor -%}</div>{%- endif -%}
    {% include visual.html type=visual data=data %}
    {%- if data.footer -%}<div class="cfg-footer">{{ data.footer }}</div>{%- endif -%}
  </div>
</section>

includes.sections/delta-section.html:
{%- comment -%}
  DELTA SECTION (a page-section type — the framing, not the table).
  The chrome a contributor gets on dropping a "Changes & Improvements section":
    · locked eyebrow "Changes & Improvements" + the locked chart-column-stacked icon
    · a required H2 heading
    · optional intro prose
    · the comparison table (the visual) in the slot
    · an optional footnote
